hreshold despite a projected #2 lineup spot and other positive factors. We also see a few wind-in warnings across the board, which could suppress offensive outcomes.\n\nThe most compelling bench decision involves **Chase Meidroth**, who posted a score of 51.88, narrowly missing a starting spot. His score was driven by a +14% boost against Seth Lugo (4.57 SP_xERA). The optimizer ultimately favored the projected lineup due to the combination of projected lineup order and slightly higher overall scores for the starting nine. **Colt Keith** and **Casey Schmitt** remain unavailable due to being on the Injured List.",
